// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
//
// The operation table: every operation of the compiler's SSA intermediate representation, one row each.
//
//     ISOLINE_OPERATION(Name, "text", Operands, ResultRule, Effect, ImmediateSchema)
//
// Name             the Operation enumerator.
// "text"           its name in the Printer's text: a WebAssembly numeric instruction keeps the text
//                  format's name, every other operation is spelled in snake case. Unique.
// Operands         the OperandSignature enumerator naming its operands: a fixed list of operand types,
//                  or that list followed by any number of further values (the *Variadic rows).
// ResultRule       the ResultRule enumerator naming its results: none, one of a fixed type, one of its
//                  first operand's type, one of the type its `type` immediate names, or any number.
// Effect           the Effect enumerator naming what it does besides computing its results, which the
//                  passes and the selector read to decide what may be removed, reordered or merged.
// ImmediateSchema  the ImmediateSchema enumerator naming its immediates, field by field.
//
// Adding an operation is adding a row here: the Operation enum, OperationTable, nameOf(), effectOf(),
// the verifier's checks and the Printer are all generated from or driven by it. The file has no
// include guard; each includer defines ISOLINE_OPERATION.

// What compact() drops: a removed instruction, still listed in its block until then. The zero value,
// so that a value-initialized Instruction is one.
ISOLINE_OPERATION(Removed, "removed", Variadic, Multiple, Pure, None)

// Constants, then one row per WebAssembly scalar numeric instruction, in Opcodes.def's order. A float
// constant's immediate is its bit pattern.
ISOLINE_OPERATION(I32Const, "i32.const", None, I32, Pure, Value)
ISOLINE_OPERATION(I64Const, "i64.const", None, I64, Pure, Value)
ISOLINE_OPERATION(F32Const, "f32.const", None, F32, Pure, Value)
ISOLINE_OPERATION(F64Const, "f64.const", None, F64, Pure, Value)
